course: dictionary
lesson: 2280
title: Words about goodbye: cremation
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about big life events, like being born or saying goodbye to someone who has died. When you read a text about these, the words around a new word give clues. «After a person dies, families care for the body in one of two main ways: burial, where the coffin is lowered into a grave, or cremation.» Here the two choices are burial and cremation, so cremation must be the other way of caring for a body.
explain: The next part gives more clues: «cremation, where the body is turned to soft grey ashes by great heat at a crematorium.» Burial puts the body in the ground, and cremation turns it to ashes. So cremation means burning a dead person's body to ashes, as a respectful way of saying goodbye. Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: does «families care for the body in one of two main ways: burning it to ashes» still make sense? Yes, it does.
explain: The word can also name an event. «After a cremation the ashes are given to the family in an urn.» Here cremation is the whole ceremony at the crematorium, not just the burning. Words can change a little in meaning depending on the sentence, so read the words around them carefully.
fact: Cremation means burning a dead person's body to ashes.
fact: Cremation is a respectful way of saying goodbye, as an alternative to burial.
fact: A cremation can also mean the ceremony or event when this happens, often at a crematorium after a funeral service.
fact: After a cremation, the ashes may be kept in an urn, buried, or scattered in a place the person loved.
fact: Different faiths have different customs, and many families choose burial or cremation together.
exercise: «After a person dies, families care for the body in one of two main ways: burial or cremation.» What is cremation? | Digging a hole and putting the body in the ground | *Burning the body to ashes as a respectful goodbye | Keeping the body in a warm house | Sending the body across the sea
exercise: «After a cremation the ashes are given to the family in an urn.» What do the family receive after a cremation? | *Ashes in an urn | A letter from the crematorium | A wooden coffin | A grave with a headstone
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the special place where cremation happens. | *crematorium | ashes | coffin | urn
test: What does burial mean? | Burning the body to ashes | *Putting the coffin into a grave in the ground | Scattering ashes on the sea | Giving the body to a museum
test: «The ashes may be buried, kept or scattered somewhere the person loved.» What does scattered mean here? | Kept safe in a box | Carried to a hospital | Put into the ground in a hole | *Spread out in many small pieces over a place
exam: Why does the text say «the person cannot feel anything» after a cremation? | Because they are asleep | Because the heat is cold | *Because their body has already stopped working | Because the family is not there
